 784:FreeRTOS/src/tasks.c **** /*
 785:FreeRTOS/src/tasks.c ****  * Convert the snprintf return value to the number of characters
 786:FreeRTOS/src/tasks.c ****  * written. The following are the possible cases:
 787:FreeRTOS/src/tasks.c ****  *
 788:FreeRTOS/src/tasks.c ****  * 1. The buffer supplied to snprintf is large enough to hold the
 789:FreeRTOS/src/tasks.c ****  *    generated string. The return value in this case is the number
 790:FreeRTOS/src/tasks.c ****  *    of characters actually written, not counting the terminating
 791:FreeRTOS/src/tasks.c ****  *    null character.
 792:FreeRTOS/src/tasks.c ****  * 2. The buffer supplied to snprintf is NOT large enough to hold
 793:FreeRTOS/src/tasks.c ****  *    the generated string. The return value in this case is the
 794:FreeRTOS/src/tasks.c ****  *    number of characters that would have been written if the
 795:FreeRTOS/src/tasks.c ****  *    buffer had been sufficiently large, not counting the
 796:FreeRTOS/src/tasks.c ****  *    terminating null character.
 797:FreeRTOS/src/tasks.c ****  * 3. Encoding error. The return value in this case is a negative
 798:FreeRTOS/src/tasks.c ****  *    number.
 799:FreeRTOS/src/tasks.c ****  *
 800:FreeRTOS/src/tasks.c ****  * From 1 and 2 above ==> Only when the return value is non-negative
